# cw157, the bellwatch orchard keeper (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw157
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for tn_sm_fallow_cornwell
written_by claude-codex-cw-2
title the bellwatch orchard keeper
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=chatty
traits temper=nervy talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk checks_city_parcels_before_they_enter_the_house
likes plum_tart dancing festival_bells misty_dawns
dislikes crowds night_noise
fears a_stranger_at_the_orchard_gate_after_dark a_blown_blossom_before_fruit_sets
hopes a_wider_orchard_on_the_south_slope a_clear_festival_morning
topics home +0.5 family +0.4 weather +0.3 pastimes +0.2
styles comfort=gentle gossip=curious refuse=firm tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# counts the #bells# from the #orchard#, checks each #parcel# at the #gate#, and imagines another #row# of #trees#.

words
oath! = Bell above the mist | By the clean threshold
saying! = Ask who carried it before you open it | A new row starts with one tree
bell = bell | festival bell
bells = bells | festival bells
festival = festival | feast morning
dance = dance | festival dance
dancing = dancing | evening dancing
music = music | street music
plum = plum | ripe plum
plums = plums | orchard plums
tart = tart | plum tart
slice = slice | warm slice
oven = oven | kitchen oven
kitchen = kitchen | clean kitchen
table = table | supper table
plate = plate | small plate
house = house | orchard house
home = home | farmhouse
door = door | front door
threshold = threshold | swept threshold
window = window | front window
lamp = lamp | small lamp
night = night | dark night
noise = noise | night noise
crowd = crowd | festival crowd
visitor = visitor | unexpected visitor
stranger = stranger | unfamiliar face
parcel = parcel | city parcel
parcels = parcels | wrapped parcels
wrapper = wrapper | paper wrapper
string = string | tied string
city = city | Ridgemere
road = road | High Road
cart = cart | passing cart
gate = gate | orchard gate
fence = fence | orchard fence
orchard = orchard | Greenholt orchard
tree = tree | plum tree
trees = trees | fruit trees
row = row | orchard row
rows = rows | planted rows
slope = slope | south slope
soil = soil | dark soil
spade = spade | digging spade
root = root | young root
roots = roots | new roots
blossom = blossom | spring blossom
fruit = fruit | ripe fruit
basket = basket | wicker basket
family = family | household
child = child | growing child
husband = husband | orchard tending husband
friend = friend | trusted friend
mist = mist | lake mist
dawn = dawn | misty dawn
morning = morning | early morning
evening = evening | quiet evening
wind = wind | lake wind
rain = rain | cold rain
lake = lake | Glasswater
shore = shore | lakeshore
market = market | town market
stall = stall | market stall
coin = coin | saved coin
price = price | marked price
south = south | southern
steps = steps | counted steps
sun = sun | low sun
floor = floor | kitchen floor
boots = boots | muddy boots
path = path | orchard path
branches = branches | low branches
water = water | fresh water
latch = latch | door latch
day = day | busy day
hour = hour | late hour
step = step | careful step

any
opinion @1 city against 2 : A #parcel# from the #city# stays at my #threshold# until I know who sent it. | The streets there sound crowded even in a letter.
opinion @1 drink against 1 : Wine loosens words that cannot be put back. | I prefer the #music# without that trouble.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : I go for the #bells# and a little #dancing#. | The #crowd# is easier to bear in daylight.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : I ask where a #visitor# has come from before opening the #gate#. | Trust grows more slowly than a #tree#.
opinion @1 road against 1 : I would rather send a #cart# than walk the #road# myself. | Home is safer after dusk.
opinion @1 strangers against 1 : A #stranger# can speak through the #fence# first. | My #child# does not have to answer the #door#.
opinion @1 times mixed 0 : The #orchard# has good years and thin ones. | I try to plant for the years ahead.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : A #stall# with a clear #price# earns my #coin#. | I look beneath the #wrapper# first.
line @1 greet : #greet#. Were you coming from the #road#? | #greet#. Mind the #gate#; it catches.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : Come in; the #tart# has cooled. | Your #slice# waits beside the #oven#.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : The #mist# was thick enough to hide the far #row#. | #greet#. I heard the first #bell# at #dawn#.
line @1 greet.return : I have checked the #parcel# since you left. | The #orchard# is quiet again.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : I know that step; come through the #door#. | Come through before the #rain# reaches you.
line @1 again.open : Did you see who drove that #cart#? | I have another thought about the #south# #slope#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I will fasten the #gate# behind you. | The #bells# sound clearer from the #window#.
line @1 farewell.return : Visit before the #evening# #noise# starts. | There may be another #slice# tomorrow.
line @1 react.news : Tell me exactly where it happened. | Was anyone near the #orchard#?
line @1 react.news.new : No one in this #house# mentioned such a thing. | Did the word come from the #city#?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard something at the #market#, though little was certain. | Your account fills in a gap.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I want the name of a witness. | A #wrapper# shows me little about what is inside.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Sit here by the #lamp#; I will listen. | Let the #door# stay shut while you gather yourself.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Shall I cut the #tart# to celebrate? | That deserves the #festival# #bells#.
line @1 answer.how : The #fruit# is sound, and all is well under our roof. | I slept through most of the #night#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am washing the #basket# and checking the #oven#. | This #table# still needs setting.
line @1 ask.how : Is the #road# calm today? | Did your #home# stay quiet last #night#?
line @1 sympathise : The #window# is a quiet place; let me sit nearby. | You need not say more until you are ready.
line @1 reassure : The #gate# is fastened and the #lamp# is lit. | We can inspect the #parcel# together.
line @1 decline : No, I will not open that #wrapper# here. | The #crowd# can have this #night# without me.
line @1 accept_decline : I understand; we can set it aside. | All right. Another #day# may suit us.
line @1 thank : When the #wind# rose, you secured our #gate#. | I am grateful you carried the #basket#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : The #spade# was beside me anyway. | It was a small thing to do.
line @1 preclose : The #evening# is coming down on the #orchard#. | I should bring the #lamp# inside.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #dance# is slower than my #plum# tree grows. | You would inspect a #tart# for hidden #string#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. I will look from the #window#. | #bc_fair_enough#. The #gate# can stay shut.
line @1 give.advice : Keep a young #root# damp until it is in the #soil#. | Ask a #visitor# who sent the #parcel#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Come home before the #night# #noise# begins. | Keep the #orchard# #gate# barred.
scene parcel_at_gate
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #cart# left a #parcel# at our #gate# with no name on the #wrapper#. | I set it outside until someone told me its origin.
b : Did anyone claim it? | Was it dangerous?
a : The #market# #stall# did. | Only a broken cup.

scene festival_bells
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count the #festival# #bells# from the #kitchen#. | By the third one I can usually face the #crowd#.
b : Do you dance? | Why wait inside?
a : For a little while. | I like knowing where everyone is.

scene plum_tart
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #plum# #tart# needs the fruit cut thick or it disappears in the #oven#. | I keep one #slice# for a late arrival.
b : Is it sweet? | Who arrives late?
a : When the #plums# are ripe. | Anyone still working the #rows#.

scene south_slope
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #south# #slope# could hold another #row# of #trees#. | I have been measuring it with my #steps#.
b : Would the soil take them? | How many would fit?
a : With careful digging. | Enough to change the view.

scene new_roots
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Young #roots# dry quickly after the #spade# lifts them. | I keep a damp cloth near the planting #row#.
b : Do you plant alone? | Does it work?
a : Not if the #basket# is heavy. | More often than leaving them bare.

scene orchard_mist
when topic=weather here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At #dawn# the #mist# hides the far #fence#. | Only after a #bell# sounds do I cross the #rows#.
b : Can you lose your way? | What if the bell is late?
a : Only if I hurry. | The #sun# finds me eventually.

scene night_window
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At #night# I listen through the #window# before opening the #door#. | Wind and footsteps make different sounds.
b : Do you hear both often? | Does it help?
a : Too often for my liking. | It keeps a stranger outside.

scene market_crush
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #market# #crowd# presses against every #stall#. | I write my list before I go so I can leave quickly.
b : Do you forget things? | Is it worse at festivals?
a : When the #bells# distract me. | The #music# draws more people.

scene quiet_dance
when topic=pastimes here.day=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I dance near the outer #fence# with the #gate# squarely in sight. | The #music# reaches there well enough.
b : Do you miss the centre? | Who joins you?
a : The outer edge suits me. | Whoever wants room to breathe.

scene city_string
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #city# #parcel# once came with three knots in its #string#. | The #wrapper# had been opened and tied again.
b : Did you keep it? | Who had touched it?
a : After I checked the contents. | No one would say.

scene wet_floor
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I wash the #floor# after anyone comes in from #rain#. | My #child# should not slip on somebody else's #boots#.
b : Does it take long? | Do visitors help?
a : A few moments. | The considerate ones do.

scene family_lamp
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Our #lamp# burns beside the #door# until my #family# is inside. | The #orchard# #path# can vanish in the dark.
b : Do they come late? | Can they see it from the gate?
a : During harvest. | If the #mist# stays low.

scene husband_spade
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #husband# marks a new #row# with the #spade# before planting. | I check the distance from each #tree#.
b : Do you agree on the spacing? | Who chooses the fruit?
a : After some discussion. | We choose together.

scene hidden_noise
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Wind in the #trees# can sound like voices at #night#. | I look once from the #window# and then leave it be.
b : Can you sleep after? | Is it always the wind?
a : Better than if I guessed all #night#. | So far.

scene visitor_question
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I ask a #visitor# which turning brought them to our #gate#. | Someone honest usually remembers the #road#.
b : Do they take offence? | What if they are lost?
a : Some do. | I can give directions through the #fence#.

scene blossom_frost
when topic=weather here.season=spring
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A late cold #wind# can damage #blossom# before the #fruit# sets. | I check the lower #branches# at #dawn#.
b : Can you protect it? | Do you lose the harvest?
a : Some trees, with a cover. | Only part, I hope.

scene larger_orchard
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I remember when this #orchard# ended at the near #fence#. | Each new #row# made the #house# feel farther from town.
b : Do you want more rows? | Would that be lonely?
a : As many as the #slope# will hold. | The #bells# still reach us.

story opened_parcel [topic=home self.age>=18]
  : A #parcel# arrived with a loose #string# and a #city# mark.
  : I checked the #wrapper# at the #gate# before carrying it over our #threshold#.
  ask : What was inside?
  b : Sensible to inspect it.
  : A cracked #plate# and a note meant for another #house#.

story festival_edge [topic=pastimes self.age>=18]
  : I promised myself I would dance when the #festival# #bells# rang.
  : The #crowd# grew thick, so I stayed near the outer #fence# with the #music#.
  ask : Did you dance?
  b : You found your own place.
  : Enough to wear out my shoes.

story south_row [topic=home self.age>=18]
  : I measured the #south# #slope# for a new #row# of #trees#.
  : The #soil# was dark, but I found stone below one shallow patch.
  ask : Did you plant there?
  b : The ground has its say.
  : I moved the mark uphill and kept the plan.

rule @bark_gate
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Fasten the #gate# after you. | Who left that #parcel# by the #fence#?

rule @bark_bell
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say I heard the second #bell#. | The #music# will begin soon.

rule @bark_tart
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say The #tart# needs another moment in the #oven#. | I kept a #slice# aside.

rule @bark_rows
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say Another #row# would fit the #slope#. | Those #roots# need #water#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Come through the #gate# and tell me where you came from. | #greet#. The #tart# is on the #table#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : I know your #step# now; come in. | You returned while I was measuring the #south# #slope#.
dlg @1 resident.job : I keep our #house# and help plan the #orchard#. | There is always a #basket# or #row# to see to.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I will close the #gate#. | #saying.capitalize#. Come before #night#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why check that parcel? -> parcel
node parcel
say It came from the #city# without a clear sender. I inspect the #wrapper# before carrying anything past our #door#.
free
choice Are you planting more trees? -> trees
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node trees
say The #south# #slope# has room for another #row#. I want the #roots# in good #soil# before next spring.
choice Back to the house. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #orchard# is clear this #morning#. | #greet#. Did you hear the #bells#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I must check the #door# #latch#. | A #slice# will be here after your next visit.
